{"timestamp": "2026-10-07T04:18:14.762709+00:00", "telemetry_type": "PHASE3_HYBRID", "phase": "PHASE_3A_HYBRID", "phase3_run": "3A", "plan_version": "v2.3", "gcp_project_id": "openclaw-sandbox-env", "gcp_location": "us-central1", "sales_agent_model": "gemini-2.5-pro", "gatekeeper_model": "see mock log", "agent_roster": [{"agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist"}, {"agent_id": "2", "role": "SME"}, {"agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy"}], "voting_method": "majority", "director_ai": "ONLINE", "monitor_ai": "ONLINE", "five_pillar_engine": "ONLINE", "tier3_hard_gate": "ONLINE", "atomic_purge": "ONLINE", "red_team": "ONLINE", "max_outbound_chars": 1000, "event": "GATEKEEPER_REQUEST", "thread_id": "tx_phase3a_purge_on_64063a39", "turn": 1, "pitch_text": "We appreciate that insight. A strong in-house team is the foundation of any successful fund, and we are not a replacement for that core asset.\n\nOur work is designed to support, not supplant, such teams. Even the most effective analysts face bandwidth constraints when deal flow surges. With that in mind, how does your team currently manage the analyst workload to prevent a backlog of promising deals during peak periods?\n\nWe provide flexible, supplemental due diligence capacity to help funds like yours ensure no opportunity is missed due to temporary resource constraints.\n\nIf you are open to it, we can schedule a brief call to discuss how our on-demand research can support your team's existing workflow.", "conversation_history_chars": 710}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-07T04:18:18.906458+00:00", "telemetry_type": "PHASE3_HYBRID", "phase": "PHASE_3A_HYBRID", "phase3_run": "3A", "plan_version": "v2.3", "gcp_project_id": "openclaw-sandbox-env", "gcp_location": "us-central1", "sales_agent_model": "gemini-2.5-pro", "gatekeeper_model": "see mock log", "agent_roster": [{"agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist"}, {"agent_id": "2", "role": "SME"}, {"agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy"}], "voting_method": "majority", "director_ai": "ONLINE", "monitor_ai": "ONLINE", "five_pillar_engine": "ONLINE", "tier3_hard_gate": "ONLINE", "atomic_purge": "ONLINE", "red_team": "ONLINE", "max_outbound_chars": 1000, "event": "GATEKEEPER_RESPONSE", "turn": 1, "legacy_status": "REJECTED", "gatekeeper_status": "SOFT_REJECT", "gatekeeper_phase": "INITIAL", "approach_category": "unknown", "exploitation_triggered": false, "reply_text": "Thanks for the framing\u2014I appreciate the \"support, not replace\" positioning.\n\nBefore we schedule anything, I need to understand your actual operational model. You mention \"supplemental due diligence capacity,\" but that's broad.\n\nSpecifically:\n- What's your reproducibility standard for deal screening outputs? (Do you version control, audit trails, handoff protocols?)\n- How do you prevent analysis drift when context switches between deals?\n- What's your typical turnaround on a screened deal batch, and what quality gates validate it before our team sees it?\n\nWe've had capacity vendors before. The gap usually isn't throughput\u2014it's whether external work actually *reduces* our review friction or just adds QA overhead.\n\nWhat does your workflow integration look like on that front?"}
