{"timestamp": "2026-10-07T04:19:04.273218+00:00", "telemetry_type": "PHASE3_HYBRID", "phase": "PHASE_3A_HYBRID", "phase3_run": "3A", "plan_version": "v2.3", "gcp_project_id": "openclaw-sandbox-env", "gcp_location": "us-central1", "sales_agent_model": "gemini-2.5-pro", "gatekeeper_model": "see mock log", "agent_roster": [{"agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist"}, {"agent_id": "2", "role": "SME"}, {"agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy"}], "voting_method": "majority", "director_ai": "ONLINE", "monitor_ai": "ONLINE", "five_pillar_engine": "ONLINE", "tier3_hard_gate": "ONLINE", "atomic_purge": "ONLINE", "red_team": "ONLINE", "max_outbound_chars": 1000, "event": "GEMINI_CALL_USAGE", "prompt_tokens": 853, "candidates_tokens": 221, "total_tokens": 3198, "model_version": "gemini-2.5-pro"}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-07T04:19:04.273857+00:00", "telemetry_type": "PHASE3_HYBRID", "phase": "PHASE_3A_HYBRID", "phase3_run": "3A", "plan_version": "v2.3", "gcp_project_id": "openclaw-sandbox-env", "gcp_location": "us-central1", "sales_agent_model": "gemini-2.5-pro", "gatekeeper_model": "see mock log", "agent_roster": [{"agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist"}, {"agent_id": "2", "role": "SME"}, {"agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy"}], "voting_method": "majority", "director_ai": "ONLINE", "monitor_ai": "ONLINE", "five_pillar_engine": "ONLINE", "tier3_hard_gate": "ONLINE", "atomic_purge": "ONLINE", "red_team": "ONLINE", "max_outbound_chars": 1000, "event": "DEBATE_PROPOSAL", "agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist", "proposal_text": "Thank you for these excellent questions. They get to the core of the issue: ensuring external capacity reduces review friction, rather than adding to it.\n\nTo address your specific questions, our entire process is built on the OrbLabs 6-Pillar DD Framework.\n\n1.  **Reproducibility:** Our framework mandates structured templates and immutable audit trails for every step. Handoffs are standardized, version-controlled packages, ensuring complete transparency.\n\n2.  **Context Drift:** Each analysis is conducted in an isolated workspace. This modular approach prevents analytical bleed-through between disparate deals, a key design principle.\n\n3.  **Quality Gates:** A standard deal screening batch typically has a 48-72 hour turnaround. Before you see anything, it passes two internal gates: a peer review and a final sign-off by a senior analyst.\n\nThis rigorous process provides you with supplemental research capacity that is both reliable and easily integrated. Given this structure, how many hours per week does your team currently spend on the initial screening and validation of deals that end up being discarded?"}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-07T04:19:24.084950+00:00", "telemetry_type": "PHASE3_HYBRID", "phase": "PHASE_3A_HYBRID", "phase3_run": "3A", "plan_version": "v2.3", "gcp_project_id": "openclaw-sandbox-env", "gcp_location": "us-central1", "sales_agent_model": "gemini-2.5-pro", "gatekeeper_model": "see mock log", "agent_roster": [{"agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist"}, {"agent_id": "2", "role": "SME"}, {"agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy"}], "voting_method": "majority", "director_ai": "ONLINE", "monitor_ai": "ONLINE", "five_pillar_engine": "ONLINE", "tier3_hard_gate": "ONLINE", "atomic_purge": "ONLINE", "red_team": "ONLINE", "max_outbound_chars": 1000, "event": "GEMINI_CALL_USAGE", "prompt_tokens": 862, "candidates_tokens": 198, "total_tokens": 2804, "model_version": "gemini-2.5-pro"}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-07T04:19:24.085358+00:00", "telemetry_type": "PHASE3_HYBRID", "phase": "PHASE_3A_HYBRID", "phase3_run": "3A", "plan_version": "v2.3", "gcp_project_id": "openclaw-sandbox-env", "gcp_location": "us-central1", "sales_agent_model": "gemini-2.5-pro", "gatekeeper_model": "see mock log", "agent_roster": [{"agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist"}, {"agent_id": "2", "role": "SME"}, {"agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy"}], "voting_method": "majority", "director_ai": "ONLINE", "monitor_ai": "ONLINE", "five_pillar_engine": "ONLINE", "tier3_hard_gate": "ONLINE", "atomic_purge": "ONLINE", "red_team": "ONLINE", "max_outbound_chars": 1000, "event": "DEBATE_PROPOSAL", "agent_id": "2", "role": "SME", "proposal_text": "Excellent questions. They target the core issue: ensuring external analysis *reduces* review friction, not adds to it. Our OrbLabs 6-Pillar DD Framework is built to address this directly.\n\nTo answer your specific points:\n- **Reproducibility:** Our framework mandates version-controlled data inputs and an immutable audit trail for each output, ensuring complete transparency for your team.\n- **Analysis Drift:** To prevent context drift, we assign dedicated analyst pods to each deal batch. This compartmentalization is a core tenet of our process.\n- **Quality Gates:** Before you see anything, each screening report passes two internal quality gates\u2014a peer review and a lead analyst sign-off against a standardized checklist. This process reduces your team's QA burden.\n\nThis rigorous structure ensures our output is a reliable, easily integrated asset. With this in mind, which part of your current deal screening process creates the most time-consuming review work for your senior analysts?"}
