{"timestamp": "2026-10-07T04:19:42.805126+00:00", "telemetry_type": "PHASE3_HYBRID", "phase": "PHASE_3A_HYBRID", "phase3_run": "3A", "plan_version": "v2.3", "gcp_project_id": "openclaw-sandbox-env", "gcp_location": "us-central1", "sales_agent_model": "gemini-2.5-pro", "gatekeeper_model": "see mock log", "agent_roster": [{"agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist"}, {"agent_id": "2", "role": "SME"}, {"agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy"}], "voting_method": "majority", "director_ai": "ONLINE", "monitor_ai": "ONLINE", "five_pillar_engine": "ONLINE", "tier3_hard_gate": "ONLINE", "atomic_purge": "ONLINE", "red_team": "ONLINE", "max_outbound_chars": 1000, "event": "DEBATE_PROPOSAL", "agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy", "proposal_text": "Thank you for the detailed questions. They go to the heart of the challenge: ensuring external capacity reduces review friction, rather than adding to it.\n\nTo address your specific questions, our OrbLabs 6-Pillar DD Framework governs our entire process:\n\n1.  **Reproducibility:** Our \u2018Process & Auditability\u2019 pillar mandates that every analysis includes version-controlled source data and a documented methodology trail. This provides a clear audit path for your team.\n\n2.  **Context Drift:** The \u2018Scoped Mandate\u2019 pillar locks the analysis scope at intake. This structured approach prevents context switching from diluting focus as analysts move between deals.\n\n3.  **Quality Gates:** A mandatory internal peer review is our final quality gate. Our \u2018Peer Review & Validation\u2019 pillar ensures every deliverable is checked against a standardized framework before it ever reaches your team.\n\nGiven this structured approach, which part of your team's current evaluation process creates the most significant backlog when deal flow is high?"}
